      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Historically, public pressure, advocacy, and institutions have often limited totalitarianism, but it's true that the current trends don't provide much hope. Potential countermeasures could involve incorporating robust checks-and-balances into national cybersecurity frameworks, as well as promoting international standards for digital rights. In it's very inception, the internet was seen as a 'global commons' by many key architects.",
